<title>JAPAN: Bank of Thailand summons bankers -- Tokyo bankers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Thailand summons bankers -- Tokyo bankers.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand (BOT) has summoned bankers in Bangkok to make an &quot;important announcement&quot; from around 8 a.m. local time on Wednesday (0100 GMT), Japanese bankers in Tokyo said.</p>
<p>They said the content of announcement was not known, but that they had heard it may be related to BOT's attempt to defend the Thai baht after its May turmoil.  </p>
<p>Some traders speculated that the BOT might be ready to devalue the currency, or to make some move on interest rates.</p>
<p>Recent market speculation has been that the BOT will opt for currency reform rather than a devaluation of the baht.</p>
<p>Traders said the central bank may also shake up the basket of currencies against which the baht is pegged.</p>
</text>
